"section": "What it does with a VCF",
"url": "index.html#how",
"text": "Steps 1 to 3 need no reads. A BAM or CRAM only adds step 4, which turns \"these two changes are in one codon\" into \"these two changes are on one molecule\". 1 Decompose Each record's REF and ALT into the changes it holds: SNVs, MNVs, insertions, deletions, delins. 2 Place Each change in its gene and codon, from a GFF or a gene table, on either strand and across exons. 3 Translate The whole codon, in one of nine NCBI genetic codes, and each indel against the protein. 4 Count With reads: how many carry each change, on which strand, and whether the changes travel together. 5 Write A TSV, a VCF with ANN , BCF on request, and a report that opens offline. How get_MNV tells one molecule from two · Indels and local haplotypes"
