"url": "getting-started/index.html#6-get-a-report-you-can-send",
"text": "The same run writes a single self-contained HTML file: get_mnv \\   --vcf G35894.var.snp.vcf \\   --fasta MTB_ancestor.fas \\   --genes anot_genes.txt \\   --bam G35894.demo.bam \\   --report sample.html The interactive HTML report get_MNV writes: summary counts, consequence breakdown, search and a variant matrix The interactive HTML report get_MNV writes: summary counts, consequence breakdown, search and a variant matrix The report opens in any browser with no server and travels as one attachment. It records the exact command that produced it along the top. It is searchable and filterable, breaks the calls down by Sequence Ontology term (here 476 missense, 320 synonymous, 134 intergenic, 10 stop gained, 1 stop lost), and draws a variant matrix across the contig. For a cohort already processed one sample per run, build one report from the existing outputs with --report-from run1.MNV.tsv run2.MNV.tsv --report cohort.html."
